<title>FRANCE: U.S principal destination for Paris Oct 96 exports.</title>
<headline>U.S principal destination for Paris Oct 96 exports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States was the principal country of destination for export traffic handled at the Paris airports in October 1996, Paris airport authority, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>The 20 leading destinations by country for ADP exports in October 1996, with percentage change on October 1995, were as follows:</p>
<p> 1  United States	   11,254 tonnes  down  7.1pct</p>
<p> 2  Japan			2,688 tonnes  down 27.6</p>
<p> 3  Hong Kong		  2,357 tonnes  up   11.9</p>
<p> 4  Germany		    2,199 tonnes  up   61.4</p>
<p> 5  Canada		     1,701 tonnes  down 25.3</p>
<p> 6  United Kingdom	   1,570 tonnes  down  8.6</p>
<p> 7  United Arab Emirates   1,459 tonnes  up   30.0</p>
<p> 8  Brazil		     1,410 tonnes  up   23.8</p>
<p> 9  India			1,373 tonnes  up   19.6</p>
<p> 10 Mexico City		1,160 tonnes  up   23.5</p>
<p> 11 Reunion		    1,008 tonnes  up    0.9</p>
<p> 12 French West Indies	 917 tonnes  down  1.9</p>
<p> 13 Egypt			  899 tonnes  up   16.2</p>
<p> 14 Italy			  846 tonnes  down  0.6</p>
<p> 15 Saudi Arabia		 838 tonnes  down 23.7</p>
<p> 16 Singapore		    741 tonnes  up   11.4</p>
<p> 17 Thailand		     709 tonnes  down 22.1</p>
<p> 18 Korea			  681 tonnes  up   13.6</p>
<p> 19 China			  639 tonnes  down 27.0</p>
<p> 20 Lebanon			607 tonnes  down 24.7</p>
<p> Total			  35,056 tonnes</p>
<p>Global October 1996 export traffic from the Paris airports, totalled 51,649 tonnes, down 3.1 percent on the same month last year, ADP said.</p>
<p>- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
